  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/Supprocom/MathBlocks",
  "published": "2026-11-02T06:52:53.19Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Adds 200 operations, for 537 in all, each implemented on CoreCLR and CUDA with bit-identical results within the documented CUDA limits: window forms (`window.*`, `window-accurate.*`) and elementwise forms (`elementwise.*`), each with a validity sibling that marks which rows are valid. Adds batched window evaluation (`MathBlocksWindowBatch`), fused expressions (`MathBlockFusedExpression`), and causality metadata for every standard operation (`MathBlockOperation.Causality`). OpenMath and Formula Interchange Profile 2 maps all 537 operations; Profile 1 is unchanged. Breaking: the CPU execution API is renamed to CoreCLR (`MathBlocksCoreCLRWorker`, `EvaluateCoreCLR`), with no aliases. CUDA execution uses the installed NVIDIA driver and CUDA Toolkit 12.0 or later; the package ships no native binaries.",
